   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = 3 x^{2} - 6 x + 4 \\). Compute the average rate of change of f over each of the intervals \\( [4, 4.100] \\), \\( [4, 4.010] \\), \\( [4, 4.001] \\), and use them to find the instantaneous rate of change of f at \\( x = 4 \\).",
      "command_verb": "estimate"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 18
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The average rate over \\( [4, 4 + h] \\) is \\( \\frac{f(4 + h) - f(4)}{h} \\), which for h = 0.1, 0.01 and 0.001 gives 18.300, 18.030, 18.003.",
         "rule_named": "average rate of change"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "As the intervals shrink the averages approach 18, so the instantaneous rate at \\( x = 4 \\) is 18. Each average is only an approximation of it.",
         "mathjson": 18,
         "rule_named": "instantaneous rate as the limit of average rates"
      }
   ],
